From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:32:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: sun60i-a733: Add the Allwinner A733 PCIe host controller

The A733 has one PCIe controller, a DesignWare core with a single lane
through the second combo PHY. Add a host driver for it on top of the
DesignWare host code, which handles the iATU, the integrated MSI
receiver and the configuration accesses.

The driver adds what is Allwinner's: the clocks, the three resets in the
order power-up, controller, ITS, the PHY, the slot supply and PERST#,
and the LTSSM control and link status in the application registers
(A733 user manual V1.00, 18.3.8.55 and 18.3.8.63). PERST# is released
PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS after the supply and the PHY reference clock are on.
A warm start can find the controller out of reset and the application
registers changed, so the resets are asserted before they are released,
the device type is set to root complex before the LTSSM starts, and
APP_DBI_RO_WR_DISABLE (18.3.8.55) is cleared before the DesignWare core
programs the port: while it is set, DBI_RO_WR_EN reads 0 whatever
dw_pcie_dbi_ro_wr_en() writes, and every write to a read-only register,
such as the class code or a capability removal, is lost.

link_up() reads Data Link Layer Link Active from the Link Status
register through the DBI, not the link-up bits of SII_INT_1. Those are
write-1-to-clear and latch (18.3.8.63), so they stay set after the link
has gone down and would report a dead link as up to the DesignWare core,
which also guards configuration accesses with it.

The AXI slave clock resets to PERI0_600M. At that rate a configuration
read through the slave window does not complete and the CPU that issued
it stalls, so the driver sets it to 400 MHz, a documented parent.

The vendor kernel has its own driver for this controller, which does
not use the DesignWare host code and brings its own iATU, MSI and
configuration code. This driver does not port it.

The driver is built in and cannot be unbound, as the Rockchip
DesignWare driver.

Not covered: the Root Port's own interrupts, link-down recovery,
suspend, and endpoint mode.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the host bound, the link
came up at Gen3 x1, and the NVMe endpoint enumerated and read back
identical data in two direct reads; no warm start was provoked.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig            |  14 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c | 362 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 377 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-sun60i-a733.c

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
index dcfbe7e229fd..1f73346f7f34 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig
@@ -487,6 +487,20 @@ config PCIE_STM32_EP
 	  This driver can also be built as a module. If so, the module
 	  will be called pcie-stm32-ep.
 
+config PCIE_SUN60I_A733
+	bool "Allwinner A733 PCIe controller (host mode)"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on OF
+	depends on PCI_MSI
+	select PCIE_DW_HOST
+	help
+	  Enables support for the DesignWare-based PCIe controller of the
+	  Allwinner A733 SoC in host mode. The controller has one lane,
+	  which the second combo PHY of the SoC carries, so the PHY driver
+	  PHY_SUN60I_A733_PCIE_COMBO is needed as well.
+
+	  Say Y here if the board has a PCIe device or slot on the A733.
+
 config PCI_DRA7XX
 	tristate
 
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile
index d4f88cfc6229..ed99caae8a85 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_PCIE_RCAR_GEN4) += pcie-rcar-gen4.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_PCIE_SPACEMIT_K1) += pcie-spacemit-k1.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_PCIE_STM32_HOST) += pcie-stm32.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_PCIE_STM32_EP) += pcie-stm32-ep.o
